    },
    "body": "Affects `ConversationListAdapter.<init>` in `app/src/main/java/org/jimvixx/smsecure/ConversationListAdapter.java`.\n\nThe conversation list adapter currently creates its digest with `SHA1` when deriving stable IDs. That algorithm is outside the `MessageDigestSpec` allow-list, which accepts SHA-256, SHA-384, and SHA-512 variants.\n\nI changed the constructor to use `SHA-256` while preserving the digest lifecycle and stable-ID derivation structure. This is safe because the change is limited to the algorithm selection and leaves the surrounding code unchanged.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
